 "spec": "release",
 "file": "sigmas",
 "notes": "\u03c3 per part for the three valid plans (deck.md Vectors): \u0394\u00b2 per part from the Parts table, \u0394_cov = covScale + \u2308\u221a(M(M+1)/2) / 2\u2309 (release.md Round 1), \u03c3\u00b2 = \u0394\u00b2\u00b7den/(2\u00b7num) in lowest terms, \u03c3_r = n/2\u00b2\u2070 with n the least integer such that n\u00b2\u00b7q \u2265 p\u00b72\u2074\u2070 (the rational the sampler is called with), and `sigma` = round(\u03c3_r \u00d7 10\u2076) ties to even (covariance: round(\u03c3_r / covScale \u00d7 10\u2076)). A sampler called with \u03c3, or with a binary64 value, is non-conformant. The boundary cases show \u03c3\u00b2 a perfect square of a dyadic (n exactly at the bound), \u03c3\u00b2 one unit of 2\u207b\u2074\u2070 below that square (n rounds up to the same value), and \u03c3 within 2\u207b\u00b2\u2070 below an integer, where \u2308\u03c3_8\u2309 over \u03c3\u00b2 (release.md Receipts) and \u2308\u03c3_r\u2309 are both shown.",
